WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.835
-People everywhere are still
in quarantine,

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.270
and that means
it's harder to see family.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.938
But, luckily, there are still
a bunch of great ways

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.007
to stay in touch.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.240
Here to give some tips
about keeping

00:00:08.240 --> 00:00:09.875
up with loved ones,
please welcome

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:11.344
"The Tonight Show" Aunts.

00:00:11.344 --> 00:00:14.346
Hi, everybody.
-Jimmy!

00:00:14.346 --> 00:00:17.883
-Jimmy!
-Hi, Jamie. Hi, Jamie.

00:00:17.883 --> 00:00:20.153
-Oh, I love it.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:23.122
-Oh, my gosh. This is great.

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.757
Why don't you introduce
yourselves

00:00:24.757 --> 00:00:26.926
for everyone at home, please?

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.895
-Oh, okay, sure.
I'm Aunt Martha.

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:31.197
I'm the nervous one.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.432
-I'm Aunt Joan, the kooky one.

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:36.202
-And I'm drunk.

00:00:36.202 --> 00:00:37.336
-Alright, great.

00:00:37.336 --> 00:00:38.971
So, I hear you're going to
give us some tips

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:41.775
on how to stay in touch
in quarantine, right?

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.809
So why don't we dive in there.
-Okay.

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.044
Well, you know,
we're going to get to that,

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.879
but, Jimmy,
I've got a lot of questions.

00:00:46.879 --> 00:00:49.348
I'm worried.
Are you eating enough?

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:52.251
-What?
-You look thin to me.

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:55.154
You look thin.
-Yeah, do a spin for us.

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.756
-Spin.
-Alright, come on, guys.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:01:00.292
I'm not doing a spin.
-Let me see your lower half.

00:01:00.292 --> 00:01:02.795
I can't...

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.096
-Show us your meat.

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:08.868
-I don't want to --
I don't want to -- I don't --

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:13.672
-You've always been
kind of fat-skinny.

00:01:13.672 --> 00:01:15.008
It's heart-attacky.
-I'm fine.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:17.376
'Cause skinny people
can have heart attacks, too.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:21.547
-Look, I'm eating --

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:24.484
I'm eating fine, Aunt Martha.
Thank you for the concern.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.419
Now, what are some ways families

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:28.353
can stay in touch
over quarantine?

00:01:28.353 --> 00:01:30.256
Do you have any thoughts?

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.759
-Oh, Jimmy,
aunts always have thoughts.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.460
-For instance, here's a thought.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.597
Why is it you never tell me
when your program is on?

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:40.199
-My program.

00:01:40.199 --> 00:01:44.169
Aunt Sue, it's on every night at
the exact same time, my program.

00:01:44.169 --> 00:01:45.504
-Why can't I ever get it?

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.575
Tonight, I turned on my TV the
same way I always do,

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:51.010
by pressing input six times,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:53.146
then crying
and calling the fire department.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.316
-Okay.
-And still no "Tonight Show."

00:01:56.316 --> 00:01:57.616
She doesn't get
"The Tonight Show,"

00:01:57.616 --> 00:02:01.287
and, Jimmy,
I think it's Russians.

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:04.691
-Can we just get -- Can we get
to the tips, please?

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.325
People want to know how
to stay in touch

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:07.560
with loved ones, alright?

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.228
Let's focus.
-Yes.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.230
Yes. Thank you, Jimmy.
You're so disciplined.

00:02:11.230 --> 00:02:14.700
You would have made a great
doctor, but it didn't work out.

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:18.037
Okay. Now, here's a tip.

00:02:18.037 --> 00:02:23.109
When you had Scarlett Johansson
on, was she nice?

00:02:23.109 --> 00:02:28.348
-That's not -- That wasn't even
close to a tip.

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:30.883
